# 01. Document Purpose

This document defines the behavioral mechanics of AEGIS.

It specifies how:

```text
USER ACTION
      ↓
UI EVENT
      ↓
VALIDATION
      ↓
DOMAIN EVENT
      ↓
STATE TRANSITION
      ↓
PERSISTENCE
      ↓
AUDIT
      ↓
UI UPDATE
      ↓
NAVIGATION / NEXT OPERATION
```

must work throughout the system.

The purpose is to prevent a critical class of implementation errors:

> AEGIS must never look like a functioning operational system while its underlying state behaves like a collection of disconnected mock screens.

This document therefore defines the relationship between:

- user interactions
- system events
- domain state
- global state
- local UI state
- persisted state
- derived state
- navigation
- notifications
- audit records
- permissions
- errors
- real-time updates

