# 08. Universal Interaction Lifecycle

Every state-changing interaction follows:

```text
USER
 ↓
INTERACTION
 ↓
PERMISSION CHECK
 ↓
INPUT VALIDATION
 ↓
DOMAIN VALIDATION
 ↓
DOMAIN EVENT
 ↓
STATE TRANSITION
 ↓
PERSISTENCE
 ↓
AUDIT RECORD
 ↓
GLOBAL STATE UPDATE
 ↓
DERIVED STATE UPDATE
 ↓
UI UPDATE
 ↓
USER FEEDBACK
```

If any mandatory stage fails, the system must not falsely report success.

---

# 09. Read Interaction Contract

For read-only actions:

```text
USER SELECTS DATA
       ↓
LOCAL UI STATE
       ↓
RENDER SELECTED CONTEXT
```

No operational domain mutation occurs.

Example:

Selecting a case does not modify the case.

---

# 10. Navigation Contract

Navigation must be treated separately from operational state.

Example:

```text
Live Surveillance
      ↓
Threat Discovery
```

does not mean:

```text
Threat status = discovered
```

Navigation only changes the user's current view.

Operational state changes only when the appropriate domain action occurs.

---

# 11. Selection Contract

Selecting an entity changes UI context.

Example:

```text
User selects Threat A
        ↓
activeThreatId = Threat A
```

This does not change:

```text
Threat A.status
Threat A.risk
Threat A.classification
```

unless a separate authorized action occurs.

---

# 12. Filter Contract

Filtering changes presentation.

Example:

```text
User selects:
Location = Ward 3
Time = Last 24 hours
Severity = High
```

The system changes the visible dataset.

It must not mutate the underlying operational data.

