# 14. State Transition Rules

A state transition must satisfy:

```text
CURRENT STATE
      +
VALID TRIGGER
      +
AUTHORIZED ACTOR
      +
VALID CONDITIONS
      ↓
ALLOWED NEXT STATE
```

If these conditions are not satisfied:

```text
NO TRANSITION
```

The system must not silently force the state forward.

---

# 15. Invalid Transition Contract

Example:

```text
PROPOSED
   ↓
EXECUTED
```

is invalid if the domain requires:

```text
PROPOSED
   ↓
REVIEWED
   ↓
AUTHORIZED
   ↓
EXECUTING
   ↓
ACTIVE
```

The interface must prevent or reject invalid transitions.

