# 64. AEGIS Behavioral Contract

AEGIS is successful when the user can trust that:

> **What I see represents the current known operational state.**

> **What I do produces the state transition the system says it produces.**

> **What the system recommends is not confused with what has actually happened.**

> **What the system knows is not confused with what it merely suspects.**

> **What changed can be traced.**

> **What failed is not represented as successful.**

> **What one authorized user changes becomes coherent across the rest of the system.**

> **What AEGIS learns from an event can influence future preparedness.**

That is the behavioral contract of AEGIS.
